This is concerning. For the first time, a Chinese model Kimi K3 has taken #1 on the Frontend Code Arena and is scoring at or near the frontier on other benchmarks.

Meanwhile, America is tying itself in knots: politicians and bureaucrats are banning new data centers, piling on state regulations, and pushing for new federal agencies to pre-approve frontier models. This approach risks losing the AI race, as the rest of the world won’t follow rules that hinder innovation. Permissionless innovation enabled America to lead the internet and become a technological leader, and it can do the same with AI—while addressing risks in a targeted way—or watch its lead fade.

